If we do go for having a set of "official" pre fixes (I'm not convinced of
the need for this), I'd modify (2) to just add a MISC: prefix, but don't
remove anything.  Since the nonstandard prefixes will then come after the
colon, they can still be seen by the human recipients but can be ignored by
the prefix-handling software.  This means that when someone wants to use a
new prefix, they can just do it, allowing persuasion by example that the
new prefix is useful, instead of having to resort to META-discussions.

